## 2. Sensitive Data, PII & Error Redaction (`SC8`)

- **Structured Logging:** Log correlation/request IDs and operational status only. Never log access/refresh tokens, passwords, `Authorization` headers, or unmasked PII.
- **User-Facing Errors & UI Masking:** Return generic error envelopes with a correlation ID; never expose raw stack traces or internal storage errors. Mask sensitive fields in UI views and background snapshots.

---

## 3. Vetted Cryptography & Secure Randomness (`SC12`)

- **Hashing & Encryption:** {{crypto_library_contract}}
- **Randomness:** Use cryptographic random generators (`{{csprng_api}}`) for tokens, nonces, and challenges—never standard non-cryptographic PRNGs.
- **Secret Comparison:** Use constant-time comparison (`{{constant_time_compare_api}}`) when verifying signatures or digests.

